grund list — the ID catalog: every declared ID in the repo, with where it's
declared and its one-line title. The complement of `grund refs` (which lists
the citations of one ID) — `list` is the index of what you can read with `grund <ID>`.

Usage:  grund list [PATH] [--kind KIND[,KIND]...] [--selector SUBJECT] [--glob PATTERN]... [--unused]
                   [--summary | --total] [--size[=lines,words,bytes]] [--top N] [--format text|json]

With no PATH, the run covers the whole project or workspace discovered from the current directory; a PATH narrows it.

Output is one line per declared ID, `<ID>  <path>:<line>  <title>`, sorted by ID.
Stub-and-inline pairs collapse to one line; a duplicate-declared ID gets a line per home.
Size mode adds every citable section and reports selected lead/full measurement pairs.

Options:
  --kind KIND[,KIND]  only selected kinds; repeatable       e.g. grund list --kind FS,AR
  --selector SUBJECT  only one declaration/chapter selector, e.g. FS.requirements
  --glob PATTERN      only coordinates the pattern matches; repeatable  e.g. --glob 'FS-login.**'
  --unused            only declarations nothing cites yet (skips a configured E2E kind unless selected)
  --summary           one row per kind with count and home  e.g. grund list --summary
  --total             only the count of the rows             e.g. grund list --glob 'FS-*' --total
  --size[=lines,words,bytes]  coordinate lead/full sizes; bare selects all three units
  --top N             largest N leads by the first selected unit; requires --size
  --format text|json   text (default) is the table on stdout; json emits NDJSON (adds `refs` count).
  --path-base project|invocation
                       project (default) spells report paths from the config root;
                       invocation: relative to the path you passed, or the current directory if you passed none.
                       e.g. grund list docs/ --path-base=invocation
                       --path-base=invocation replaces a version-1 `[output] relative_paths = false`.
                       --format json replaces a version-1 `[output] format = "json"`; a flag outranks its key.

Exit:  0 scan succeeded (an empty catalog prints nothing) · 2 unreadable tree, an unknown --kind, or a refused --glob.

Examples:
  grund list                      # the whole catalog
  grund list --kind FS,AR docs/   # specs and architecture IDs under docs/
  grund list --summary            # counts by kind
  grund list --selector FS.requirements # every FS requirements chapter
  grund list --glob 'FS-login.**' --total # how many sections FS-login holds
  grund list --size=words --top 10 # largest coordinate leads
  grund list --unused             # uncited declarations (specs, decisions, …) — configured E2E cases excluded
  grund list --unused --kind FS   # uncited FS declarations only
  grund list --kind FS --format json # one NDJSON record per ID, with its refs count

Guide:    https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/blob/main/docs/user-facing/coordinate-sizes.md
Guide:    https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/blob/main/docs/user-facing/querying.md
Example:  https://github.com/agent-grounds/grund/tree/main/examples/review-checklist
